                <pb facs="0707" n="699" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg699"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760F.62/1306: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-29T18:00:00+01:00">September 29, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 29—2:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1647. Bonnet has just informed me the luncheon at Munich passed off in a spirit
                    of general gaiety and conciliation. There is as yet no news about the meeting at
                    4 o’clock.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
